  "query_preview": "..\n\nA closed low will track well south of the region Wednesday night \ninto Thursday. Meanwhile during this same time period a shortwavce\ntrough will track southeast from Canada into the Dakotas along the\nnorthern branch of this split flow regime with a cold front. This\nwill bring gusty northwest winds to NE Montana on Thursday though\nprecipitation chances will remain to the east with that wave.\n\nOn Friday, NBM begins to advance an upper ridge across the western\nU.S. as the closed low becomes aborbed by a deepening trough\nacross the central CONUS. This will lend to warm and dry\nconditions for the CWA Friday into Saturday, as highs return to\nthe 70s as the weekend gets underway. The next cold front will\napproach on Saturday evening.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\nNBM was used for the forecast cycle with little in the way of\ndeviations this time around due to an overall benign weather\npattern aside from consistency adjustments for collaboration with\nsurrounding offices.",
